Q: Parse a log file line containing square bracketed expressions A: <p>If you are parsing consistently formatted lines of a file, PHP has <code>fscanf()</code> which is designed for this purpose.</p>
<p>Push the qualifying content into the result array while iterating the lines of the file. <a href="https://3v4l.org/uqPS3#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$handle = fopen('your_file.log', 'r');
$result = [];
while ($captureCount = fscanf($handle, &quot;[%[^]]] [%[^]]] %[^\n]&quot;, $dateTime, $type, $message)) {
    if ($captureCount === 3) {
        $result[] = [
            'dateTime' =&gt; $dateTime,
            'type' =&gt; $type,
            'message' =&gt; $message,
        ];
    }
}
fclose($handle);
var_export($result);
</code></pre>
